### Pareto Front Assessment

The non-dominated set (no other point beats both objectives simultaneously):
- **936.62 bar / 0.27** (17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s run1) — highest modulus, but only 1 specimen survived fit, SD=0, single-run, wrinkle present → **unvalidated, high uncertainty**
- **860.94 bar / 0.28** (17p5-19deg-90s-N2-1800s run1) — high modulus, but single-run, wrinkle → **unvalidated**
- **421.45 bar / 0.44** (18-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s run3) — highest pore fraction, moderate modulus → **unvalidated** (runs 1,2,3,4,5 exist but with variable results; run3 is the best pore fraction)
- **468.22 bar / 0.40** (18-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s run5) — also high pore fraction

The 18-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s condition has 5 runs with pore fractions ranging 0.32–0.44 and moduli 339–476 bar. Run3 achieved 0.44 pore fraction — the highest in the dataset — but with high variability across runs (SD of pore fraction across runs is large). This is a Pareto-front candidate for the high-pore-fraction end.

The 17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s condition (run1: 936 bar/0.27; run2: 675 bar/0.30) shows high modulus but only 2 runs with divergent results (936 vs 675 bar), both with defects. This is a Pareto-front candidate for the high-modulus end but needs validation.

### Validation Policy Check

**17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s**: run1 gave 936 bar/0.27 (single specimen fit, SD=0, wrinkle), run2 gave 675 bar/0.30 (2 specimens, wrinkle/gap). These are independent repeats but show large divergence (936 vs 675 bar). The run1 value is a large apparent gain with SD=0 (single fit), making it unreliable. A third independent repeat is warranted to clarify whether ~900 bar is achievable.

**17p5-19deg-90s-N2-1800s**: run1 gave 860 bar/0.28 (2 specimens, wrinkle), run2 gave 549 bar/0.30 (3 specimens, wrinkle). Again large divergence. The high-modulus run is unconfirmed.

**18-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s**: 5 runs with pore fractions 0.32, 0.39, 0.44, 0.36, 0.40 and moduli 476, 340, 421, 430, 468 bar. The pore fraction is consistently high (0.32–0.44) but variable. This condition is the best for pore fraction but modulus is moderate.

### Decision

The **17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s** condition is the strongest Pareto-front candidate for high modulus (936 bar run1, 675 bar run2) with acceptable pore fraction (0.27–0.30). The two existing runs diverge substantially (936 vs 675 bar), run1 has SD=0 (single fit), and both have membrane defects. A third independent repeat is required by the validation policy before treating this as a confirmed improvement.

This is the same condition as runs 1 and 2: mixing_temp=65, bath_temp=18, pullcast_speed=10, nitrogen=true, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=75, nips_bath_wait_time=1800, polymer_wt=17.5, additive_wt=0.

