  "polymer_wt": 17.5,
  "additive_wt": 0
}
```

**Rationale:** The 17.5 wt% / bath_temp=18°C / 75s wait / N2 / 1800s NIPS condition is the leading Pareto-front candidate for high elastic modulus (run1: 936 bar, run2: 675 bar) with pore fractions of 0.27–0.30. However, the two existing runs diverge by ~260 bar — a large gap where run1 relied on a single surviving fit (SD=0) and both runs showed membrane wrinkles. The validation policy requires an independent third repeat before treating either value as confirmed. This repeat will clarify whether ~900 bar is reproducible or an outlier, establish the true mean modulus and pore fraction for this condition, and determine whether it genuinely dominates other candidates on both objectives. If confirmed near 900 bar with pore fraction ~0.27–0.30, it would represent the best high-modulus Pareto point observed. If it converges near 675 bar, it remains competitive but the search should then pivot to exploring whether bath_temp adjustments (e.g., 17–19°C) or wait time changes can simultaneously push pore fraction above 0.30 without sacrificing modulus.

