The **17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s** condition (run1: 936 bar, 0.27 PF) is the highest modulus observed. Run2 gave 675 bar / 0.30 PF — substantially lower, suggesting high run-to-run variability. Runs 4 and 5 (Oct 30) both failed to yield valid modulus/pore fraction measurements (all fits discarded, negative strain values). So we have only 2 valid modulus measurements across 5 runs, with a large spread (675 vs. 937 bar). This candidate is **not reliably confirmed** on either objective.

The **17p5-19deg-90s-N2-1800s** condition (run1: 861 bar / 0.28 PF) has only one valid measurement and run2 gave 549 bar / 0.30 — again high variability, not confirmed.

The **18-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s** high-pore-fraction candidate has 5 runs with modulus measured in runs 1, 3, 4, 5 — mean ~415 bar, pore fraction 0.32–0.44 with high SD in run2. This is partially validated but pore fraction is variable.

### What to Do Next

The **17p5-19deg-90s-N2-1800s** condition is a strong Pareto-front candidate (high modulus ~860 bar, moderate pore fraction 0.28) with only one valid measurement. It needs validation. However, runs 4 and 5 of the nearby 17p5-18deg condition failed completely (instrument/fitting issues on Oct 30), suggesting a possible equipment issue at that time rather than a process issue.

